\"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3390010099.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"87365f6e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3390010099.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3390010099.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 3423, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:31\", \"token_count\": 796, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**svrnm** — COMMENTED — 2025-11-20T18:33:12Z\\n\\n**svrnm** — APPROVED — 2025-11-20T19:18:34Z\\n\\n**trask** — APPROVED — 2025-11-20T19:24:07Z\\n\\n**maryliag** — APPROVED — 2025-11-20T20:54:14Z\\n\\n**mx-psi** — APPROVED — 2025-11-21T10:32:49Z\\n\\n**jack-berg** — APPROVED — 2025-11-21T15:57:47Z\\n\\n**tedsuo** — APPROVED — 2025-12-01T18:24:54Z\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-02]\\n\\n# Pull Request: Project Proposal: Ecosystem Explorer (open-telemetry/community#3000)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/community/pull/3000  \\n\\n**Author**: jaydeluca  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-09-19T10:11:57Z · **Updated**: 2025-12-02T08:40:24Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: merged (2025-12-01T19:04:18Z)  \\n\\n**Branch**: `instrumentation-docs` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +251 / -0 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: area/project-proposal  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Review Comments (13)\\n\\n**svrnm** on `projects/instrumentation-documentation.md` — 2025-09-19T11:58:43Z\\n\\nPersonally I would put the extraction and availability of the meta data first, and the web application second. There might be other places&tools where people would want to have that data available.\\n\\n**svrnm** on `projects/instrumentation-documentation.md` — 2025-09-19T11:59:42Z\\n\\neven if it would be a small one, I think having a dedicated SIG which is populated from Java&Comms and some other SIGs would be the way forward, and provide clear ownership.\\n\\n**svrnm** on `projects/instrumentation-documentation.md` — 2025-09-19T11:59:55Z\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"svrnm comment 2025 11 20t18 33 12z svrnm approv 2025 11 20t19 18 34z trask approv 2025 11 20t19 24 07z maryliag approv 2025 11 20t20 54 14z mx psi approv 2025 11 21t10 32 49z jack berg approv 2025 11 21t15 57 47z tedsuo approv 2025 12 01t18 24 54z sourc id src pr 02 pull request project propos ecosystem explor open telemetri communiti 3000 canon url http github com open telemetri communiti pull 3000 author jaydeluca creat 2025 09 19t10 11 57z updat 2025 12 02t08 40 24z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state merg 2025 12 01t19 04 18z branch instrument doc main chang 251 0 across 2 file label area project propos mileston review comment 13 svrnm on project instrument document md 2025 09 19t11 58 43z person i would put the extract and avail of the meta data first and the web applic second there might be other place tool where peopl would want to have that data avail svrnm on project instrument document md 2025 09 19t11 59 42z even if it would be a small one i think have a dedic sig which is popul from java comm and some other sig would be the way forward and provid clear ownership svrnm on project instrument document md 2025 09 19t11 59 55z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"id\": \"d1c12561e10f79e0\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.30875239220624556, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.14234191743749366, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6970435, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 25436, \"chunk_count\": 14, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:58\", \"token_count\": 7169, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-05]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-03\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3479626706  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-03T09:30:26Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-03T09:30:26Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-23\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n- Tyler Yahn\\n\\n- Alex Boten\\n\\n- David Ashpole (dashpole)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n### PR status: JSON/YAML unmarshalling\\n\\n- A small change (error tag) was suggested and applied.\\n\\n- Build is running; plan is to merge once green.\\n\\n### Adding env var support for OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE\\n\\nReference: Adding env var support for OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/8059\\n\\n- Goal:\\n\\n  - If the env var is present, load the indicated config file and configure the SDK automatically, minimizing user code.\\n\\n- Current ecosystem notes:\\n\\n  - PHP reports support; other languages vary (JS likely working on it; C++ explicitly not supporting).\\n\\n  - Go users are accustomed to programmatic setup; unclear if SDK-level support is necessary.\\n\\n- Go implementation options discussed:\\n\\n  - SDK experimental feature-flag approach:\\n\\n    - Use internal “x”/experimental packages to expose a feature gate for the env var.\\n\\n    - Check the env var during SDK setup (e.g., TracerProvider construction), and if enabled, configure from the file.\\n\\n    - Complications:\\n\\n      - Potential import cycles (e.g., if otelconf needs sdk and vice versa).\\n\\n      - Decision required on how to handle passed options vs. config file (ignore vs. merge).\\n\\n      - Requires similar work across trace, metrics, and logs modules.\\n\\n  - Contrib-first approach (preferred short term):\\n\\n    - Implement in opentelemetry-go-contrib/otelconf:\\n\\n      - Provide an explicit function to load from OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE and construct/return SDK providers.\\n\\n      - Optionally offer an init-based side effect that sets the global provider if the env var is set (not ideal, but acceptable during experimental phase to collect feedback).\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src note 05 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 03 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3479626706 author pellar creat 2025 11 03t09 30 26z updat 2025 11 03t09 30 26z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 23 attende tyler yahn alex boten david ashpol dashpol transcript pr status json yaml unmarshal a small chang error tag wa suggest and appli build is run plan is to merg onc green ad env var support for otel _ experiment _ config _ file refer ad env var support for otel _ experiment _ config _ file http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 8059 goal if the env var is present load the indic config file and configur the sdk automat minim user code current ecosystem note php report support other languag vari j like work on it c explicit not support go user are accustom to programmat setup unclear if sdk level support is necessari go implement option discuss sdk experiment featur flag approach use intern x experiment packag to expos a featur gate for the env var check the env var dure sdk setup e g tracerprovid construct and if enabl configur from the file complic potenti import cycl e g if otelconf need sdk and vice versa decis requir on how to handl pass option v config file ignor v merg requir similar work across trace metric and log modul contrib first approach prefer short term implement in opentelemetri go contrib otelconf provid an explicit function to load from otel _ experiment _ config _ file and construct return sdk provid option offer an init base side effect that set the global provid if the env var is set not ideal but accept dure experiment phase to collect feedback\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"873abbfe8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"id\": \"1fe86388dce9138e\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2845397384100422, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.13232721201434608, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6397023, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"873abbfe8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 4412, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:29\", \"token_count\": 1155, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"Can you share more about why you aren't able to migrate to the stats handler?  We [deprecated](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/4534) the interceptors almost 2 years ago, which seems like plenty of time to migrate.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicholasngai** — 2025-10-28T20:40:37Z\\n\\nEven if we removed all of our references, references in transitive dependencies still cause compilation errors, and we don’t have control over the timeline at which transitive dependencies remove those code references.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**dmathieu** — 2025-10-29T08:35:31Z\\n\\nThat doesn't look like a good reason to me. There will always be unmaintained transitive dependencies that prevent this kind of upgrades.\\n\\nThat's tech debt that needs to be fixed, not kept on our end.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicholasngai** — 2025-10-29T16:28:55Z\\n\\nThe question is really whether we can rely on otelgrpc to be stable! For now, we are stuck on v0.58.0 because of compilation errors on higher versions introduced by the breaking change. If there is an urgent security patch introduced, we won’t be able to upgrade to it.\\n\\nGenerally, with Golang, we avoid breaking changes aggressively avoid these kinds of things. Does maintaining this interceptor involve significant overhead from the maintainers?\\n\\n---\\n\\n**MrAlias** — 2025-10-29T17:37:26Z\\n\\nPlease do not rely on an unstable package as being stable.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicholasngai** — 2025-10-29T17:38:42Z\\n\\nAre there plans to make this package stable? Or are we sticking with [ZeroVer](https://0ver.org/) for the forseeable future?\\n\\n---\\n\\n**MrAlias** — 2025-10-29T18:06:47Z\\n\\n> Are there plans to make this package stable?\\n\\nThere is definitely desire among project contributor to progress this package towards stability. But please understand this is an open-source project. It is driven by a the dedicated effort of engineers who donate their time to working on this. That time is valuable and allocated to many efforts.\\n\\nI'm happy to add the question of stabilization to our weekly SIG meeting happening tomorrow. @nicholasngai I would strongly suggest you attend the meeting tomorrow to discuss your use-case and help motivate allocation of effort for this stabilization. I don't anticipate this stabilization happening within 2025, but I could see us prioritizing it for 2026 if we have community involvement and/or added developer help here.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"can you share more about whi you aren t abl to migrat to the stat handler we deprec http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 4534 the interceptor almost 2 year ago which seem like plenti of time to migrat nicholasngai 2025 10 28t20 40 37z even if we remov all of our refer refer in transit depend still caus compil error and we don t have control over the timelin at which transit depend remov those code refer dmathieu 2025 10 29t08 35 31z that doesn t look like a good reason to me there will alway be unmaintain transit depend that prevent this kind of upgrad that s tech debt that need to be fix not kept on our end nicholasngai 2025 10 29t16 28 55z the question is realli whether we can reli on otelgrpc to be stabl for now we are stuck on v0 580 becaus of compil error on higher version introduc by the break chang if there is an urgent secur patch introduc we won t be abl to upgrad to it general with golang we avoid break chang aggress avoid these kind of thing doe maintain this interceptor involv signific overhead from the maintain mralia 2025 10 29t17 37 26z pleas do not reli on an unstabl packag a be stabl nicholasngai 2025 10 29t17 38 42z are there plan to make this packag stabl or are we stick with zerov http 0ver org for the forseeabl futur mralia 2025 10 29t18 06 47z are there plan to make this packag stabl there is definit desir among project contributor to progress this packag toward stabil but pleas understand this is an open sourc project it is driven by a the dedic effort of engin who donat their time to work on this that time is valuabl and alloc to mani effort i m happi to add the question of stabil to our week sig meet happen tomorrow nicholasngai i would strong suggest you attend the meet tomorrow to discus your use case and help motiv alloc of effort for this stabil i don t anticip this stabil happen within 2025 but i could see u priorit it for 2026 if we have communiti involv and or ad develop help here\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874f32be8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8078.md\", \"id\": \"1afc8125e2debda9\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2711417708176356, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11229780116805087, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6417777, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8078.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874f32be8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8078.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8078.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 4910, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:12\", \"token_count\": 1517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"  - Status: PR exists; default temporality aggregation functions were not exposed; proposal includes a string-based “temporality select.”\\n\\n  - Concern: Replacing functions via string selector raised concerns.\\n\\n  - Next: No recent activity; likely to wait and potentially move out of the milestone.\\n\\n- Optimized locking for metric aggregation:\\n\\n  - Status: Work in progress by David; awaiting one more testing PR before starting locking improvements.\\n\\n  - Context: Approach reviewed informally with Josh McDonald; thought reasonably good.\\n\\n  - Testing PR: “Add concurrent-safe tests for metric aggregation” needs more reviews.\\n\\n  - Notes: A test-run issue caused confusion around time ordering; not a fundamental `time.Now` issue. Go 1.25 testing time manipulation may help if needed.\\n\\n- Exporter: Prometheus migrate to new configuration options:\\n\\n  - Status: On David’s list.\\n\\n  - Scope: Expected to be a one-line default change; no “Help Wanted” needed.\\n\\n- Improved error handling:\\n\\n  - Status: PR was in draft and author became inactive.\\n\\n  - Decision: Remove from milestone; consider pinging the author. Should not block release.\\n\\n- High mutex contention in metric sums:\\n\\n  - Status: Assigned to David; actively being fixed.\\n\\n- Observability packages:\\n\\n  - Status: Multiple PRs open and being reworked.\\n\\n  - Release impact: Not critical for upcoming release; if they block, move them out.\\n\\n  - Activity: Some PRs show movement; Tyler is actively working on one; others have limited updates.\\n\\n- Prometheus exporter: Optimize return times:\\n\\n  - Status: Worth review for those working on observability metrics.\\n\\n  - Context: Already merged for the standard trace exporter.\\n\\n  - Note: Awaiting minimum time requirement (~23 minutes) before completion.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-01]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-10-10\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3389930076  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-10T12:53:12Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-10T12:54:14Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-09-25\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n- Tyler Yahn.\\n\\n- Bryan Boreham.\\n\\n- David Ashpole (dashpole).\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"status pr exist default tempor aggreg function were not expos propos includ a string base tempor select concern replac function via string selector rais concern next no recent activ like to wait and potenti move out of the mileston optim lock for metric aggreg status work in progress by david await one more test pr befor start lock improv context approach review inform with josh mcdonald thought reason good test pr add concurr safe test for metric aggreg need more review note a test run issu caus confus around time order not a fundament time now issu go 1 25 test time manipul may help if need export prometheus migrat to new configur option status on david s list scope expect to be a one line default chang no help want need improv error handl status pr wa in draft and author becam inact decis remov from mileston consid ping the author should not block releas high mutex content in metric sum status assign to david activ be fix observ packag status multipl pr open and be rework releas impact not critic for upcom releas if they block move them out activ some pr show movement tyler is activ work on one other have limit updat prometheus export optim return time status worth review for those work on observ metric context alreadi merg for the standard trace export note await minimum time requir 23 minut befor complet sourc id src note 01 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 1010 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3389930076 author pellar creat 2025 10 10t12 53 12z updat 2025 10 10t12 54 14z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 09 25 attende tyler yahn bryan boreham david ashpol dashpol\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"872f2dca8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3389930076.md\", \"id\": \"bab18cd51375b357\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2681306858176356, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11229780116805087, \"vector_similarity\": 0.63174075, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3389930076.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"872f2dca8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3389930076.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3389930076.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 4478, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:33\", \"token_count\": 1509, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"The initial POC focused on a static-site approach which is much simpler to operate, has _almost_ no ongoing maintenance burden, and still meets our immediate needs. Personally, I'd much prefer a solution that requires as little operational overhead as possible.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**trask** — 2025-10-01T19:11:49Z\\n\\n+1 on optimizing for low operational overhead since that's an area where we struggle as an Open Source project\\n\\n---\\n\\n**thompson-tomo** — 2025-10-06T05:26:18Z\\n\\nI am all for a lower operational overhead but I do get worried when I see suggestions to build something as that can create tech debt especially when it is not a key part of the organisation business/objective. Hence suggestion to use an established product.\\n\\nWith the objective of low operational effort and static site generation in mind, we should be exploring how weaver can be contribute to the solution.\\n\\nWhat I could foresee is:\\n\\n- User defines a weaver registry file which imports signals from the sem conv registry\\n\\n- User refines the imported signals based on what they are implementing\\n\\n- User defines either a seperate implementation metadata file or adds it to the registry file. TBD\\n\\n- Weaver codegen runs ie `weaver implementation generate` for the refined signals and metadata. This would produce boilerplate code which is used in the implementation and exports a yaml definition file (resolved schema).\\n\\n- the exported yaml could be added to the eco-system which is proceeded by `weaver implementation describe` to emit the static content.\\n\\nAll of that would be reusable especially if the repo/package readme could also be generated in the same manner.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**jaydeluca** — 2025-10-06T10:17:57Z\\n\\n@thompson-tomo who is a \\\"user\\\" in your example? This project is specifically aimed at creating documentation for java instrumentation (and possibly the collector and other languages as a stretch goal). There are over 250 instrumentations in the java project, and at this time none of them use weaver to define their attributes. I have experimented with introducing weaver to the project in order to generate metrics/attributes for an instrumentation, but as of this time, there are no existing plans by the SIG to rewrite everything in that repo to use weaver (that I am aware of).\\n\\nI am all for integrating weaver where it makes sense, but if we are saying we need to convert that repo to use weaver before we move ahead with this project, I fear it would be a very long time before we could deliver anything useful. There's also a significant number of things involved here that go beyond just documenting the attributes that I don't think weaver helps with.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"the initi poc focus on a static site approach which is much simpler to oper ha _ almost _ no ongo mainten burden and still meet our immedi need person i d much prefer a solut that requir a littl oper overhead a possibl trask 2025 10 01t19 11 49z 1 on optim for low oper overhead sinc that s an area where we struggl a an open sourc project thompson tomo 2025 10 06t05 26 18z i am all for a lower oper overhead but i do get worri when i see suggest to build someth a that can creat tech debt especi when it is not a key part of the organis busi object henc suggest to use an establish product with the object of low oper effort and static site generat in mind we should be explor how weaver can be contribut to the solut what i could forese is user defin a weaver registri file which import signal from the sem conv registri user refin the import signal base on what they are implement user defin either a seper implement metadata file or add it to the registri file tbd weaver codegen run ie weaver implement generat for the refin signal and metadata this would produc boilerpl code which is use in the implement and export a yaml definit file resolv schema the export yaml could be ad to the eco system which is proceed by weaver implement describ to emit the static content all of that would be reusabl especi if the repo packag readm could also be generat in the same manner jaydeluca 2025 10 06t10 17 57z thompson tomo who is a user in your exampl this project is specif aim at creat document for java instrument and possibl the collector and other languag a a stretch goal there are over 250 instrument in the java project and at this time none of them use weaver to defin their attribut i have experi with introduc weaver to the project in order to generat metric attribut for an instrument but a of this time there are no exist plan by the sig to rewrit everyth in that repo to use weaver that i am awar of i am all for integr weaver where it make sens but if we are say we need to convert that repo to use weaver befor we move ahead with this project i fear it would be a veri long time befor we could deliv anyth use there s also a signific number of thing involv here that go beyond just document the attribut that i don t think weaver help with\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"id\": \"99d77b00ebd65a06\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.26718870664927485, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10014705521324983, \"vector_similarity\": 0.65695256, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 25436, \"chunk_count\": 14, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:58\", \"token_count\": 7169, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}], \"pagination\": {\"page\": 1, \"page_size\": 10, \"total_chunks\": 68, \"total_pages\": 7}, \"query_info\": {\"question\": \"Ecosystem Explorer project status implementation progress completed 2026\", \"similarity_threshold\": 0.2, \"vector_weight\": 0.3, \"keyword_search\": false, \"dataset_count\": 1}}"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"No. The evidence shows an initial Ecosystem Explorer proof of concept already existed when the proposal was opened on September 19, 2025; the proposal merged later, on December 1, 2025. The dataset does not show a separate post-merge implementation delivery. [SRC-PR-02](https://github.com/open-telemetry/community/pull/3000)"}}
